{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["And it came to pass after these things — everywhere that is said: 'after these things,' it is connected to the preceding passage. 'After these things,' when Avram defeated the kings, the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: ״Fear not, Avram,״ from the nations. 'And it came to pass after these things,' that Yitzhak was born and it was told to Avraham, saying, etc., ״ובתואל ילד את רבקה״. And likewise 'after these things,' that Mordecai reported about Bigthan and Teresh — King Ahasuerus promoted Haman, who wanted to kill Mordecai, and what benefited him was that he had saved the king, and Haman was hanged. So too here: after the things that Avraham cut a covenant with Avimelech — to him, to his grandson, and to Avraham's grandson — and he gave him seven ewe-lambs, the wrath of the Holy One, blessed be He, was kindled over this, for the land of the Philistines had been given to Avraham, and also in Joshua they cast lots over the cities of the five lords of the Philistines as part of the territory of Israel, and the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded them ״לא תחיה כל נשמה״. Therefore —" "And ha-Elohim tested Avraham — provoked and afflicted him, as written: ״הנסה דבר אליך תלאה״; ״על נסותם את ה׳״; ״מסה ומריבה״; ״בחנני ה׳ ונסני״. That is to say: 'You grew proud over the son I gave you, to cut a covenant between you and between their children — and now, go and offer him up as a burnt-offering, and see what your covenant-cutting accomplished!' And so I found afterward in the M(egillah?) of Shmuel: ״ויהי ארון ה׳ בארץ פלשתים שבעה חדשים״. He wrote: ״את שבע כבשות הצאן תקח מידי״. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: 'You gave him seven ewe-lambs — by your life, his sons will wage seven wars against your sons and defeat them.' Another interpretation: 'By your life, his sons will slay seven righteous men among your sons, and these are they: Shimshon, Hophni, and Pinhas, Shaul, and his three sons.' Another interpretation: 'By your life, his sons will destroy seven sanctuaries, and these are they: the Tent of Meeting, and Gilgal, Nov, and Shiloh, and Givon, and the Eternal House — two.' Another interpretation: the Ark wandered through the field of the Philistines seven months." "נסה — kontres Ari'ah."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :register {:flags {1 ["the Eternal"]}}, :notes {0 "Reading לנינו ולנכדו as 'to his grandson and to Avraham's grandson' based on Genesis 21:23 where Avimelech's party includes descendants; the phrase is textually difficult.", 1 "The phrase במ׳ של שמואל likely refers to the book of Samuel (מ״ש). The closing תרין 'two' beside בית עולמים is textually difficult; rendered as found.", 2 "This appears to be a cross-reference to a work or manuscript identified as 'Kontres Ari'ah'; the reference is opaque and rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:44:55.901355466Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}